Description:
The summary:
<br />
<br />[spoiler]- George isn't tragically asking how he's going to get the letter out of there, he's just grumbling about it being stuck in the back (and at the end of the event notes that he should stop forgetting his reach extender) (the implication is that as Penny approaches he's stuck trying to fish it out, making Penny think she should help);
<br />
<br />- George is initially more baffled than mad about what Penny did, and heats up as he keeps talking (and is even more offended by the implication that he can't do things on his own than the physical rudeness, though he doesn't say that);
<br />
<br />- It takes Penny some time to understand what exactly went wrong, at first she's just upset that her efforts aren't appreciated for what they're meant to be;
<br />
<br />- As the farmer, you have a choice between being nice to Penny in a way that makes her feel better even as you take George's side overall, being mean to Penny in a way that makes her more upset but cheers George up a bit, and choosing to stay out of it. Penny's responses ultimately converge in a way that hopefully naturally segues into the rest of the dialogue;
<br />
<br />- After Penny apologizes, George finally cools off and acknowledges that she was just trying to help, although he doesn't either apologize to her (because he was right) or thank her (because he's grumpy and bitter and doesn't like to be reminded of his limitations and how other people perceive him, as well as because he didn't want the help);
<br />
<br />- Penny continues to feel bad about what happened, because she's ultimately an empathetic and nice young woman who took this whole situation very personally.
<br />
<br />The "we should respect our elders" dialogue plays out the same way as in vanilla.[/spoiler]
<br />
<br />Unlike my Robin/Demetrius mod, screenshots feature just highlights, not every single thing that happens in the event.
<br />
<br />Should be compatible with other mods that edit Penny's dialogue by overwriting them for this specific instance. Compatible with SVE but no other map change mods yet.
